  "notes": [
    "three levels below the lobby, under both towers: its western rooms, from Vinings and Williams to Marietta and the Heritage Boardroom, are under the International Tower and its ballroom; the rest are under the Atrium Tower",
    "the hotel's plan of this level (p. 3) is drawn half a turn round from its other pages; it is turned back here, and both elevator banks and both escalators then fall where the levels above put them",
    "Courtland is 39.8 x 48 and Dunwoody 37 x 48: the table gives each the other's width, against its own square footage and the plan",
    "Dragon Con's map labels Courtland and Dunwoody the other way round from the hotel's plan; the hotel's is drawn - to be checked in person",
    "the Heritage Boardroom has no dimensions in the table; 15 x 26 is the plan's",
    "where the International Tower stands, 134 ft west and 107 ft south of the atrium elevators, is read from this level's plan alone: no other page draws both towers"
